  data: {
    LLM: "In Football, a 'Natural' hand is almost never enough to win. You must aim for at least Four-of-a-Kind. If you don't start with a wild card (3 or 6) or a high pair, fold early.\n\nInventory Management: Because 2s give extra cards, having a 2 face-up is a huge advantage. It gives you a wider selection of cards to form your final 5ndcard hand, effectively increasing your 'draw' potential.\n\nThe 'Scoreboard' Bluff: If your up-cards include two 6s or two 3s (which are wild), opponents will assume you have at least a Full House or better. Use this visible strength to push players off hands that might actually be stronger in the hole.",
    Player: "In Football, a 'Natural' hand is almost never enough to win. You must aim for at least Four-of-a-Kind. If you don't start with a wild card (3 or 6) or a high pair, fold early.\n\nInventory Management: Because 2s give extra cards, having a 2 face-up is a huge advantage. It gives you a wider selection of cards to form your final 5ndcard hand, effectively increasing your 'draw' potential.\n\nThe 'Scoreboard' Bluff: If your up-cards include two 6s or two 3s (which are wild), opponents will assume you have at least a Full House or better. Use this visible strength to push players off hands that might actually be stronger in the hole.",
